  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on calculating an aspiration level (-500) and comparing outcomes to it, favoring the lottery with a higher chance of exceeding this level. Lottery A has a 50% chance of a positive difference (+500), while B has 0%. The individual’s verbal report does not mention any calculation of an average outcome, nor do they reference a psychological reference point derived from all possible outcomes. Instead, their reasoning is based on the aversiveness of a certain loss and a threshold for when such a loss would be acceptable (only if the alternative were much worse). This reflects loss aversion or a form of minimax reasoning rather than an aspiration level based on the mean of all outcomes. There is no indication that the individual computed or used the mean of all outcomes as a reference point, nor that they evaluated how often each lottery exceeds such a point. The justification is grounded in avoiding sure losses, not in exceeding an aspiration level derived from averaging outcomes. Therefore, the reasoning process described does not align with the specified decision reason.",
